  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "Qt: Improve field autocompletion in DisplayFilterEdit",
  "description": "The current logic does not make sense, because test_df is NULL whenever\nthe filter fails, and so the test for the type of error never applies.\n\nWe only want to offer field autocompletion when the current token can\nbe a field in the filter grammar. We look at the preamble; if the\npreamble is empty, a field can start a filter. If the preamble does\nnot compile as a valid filter, but the error is the preamble is a\nfilter that ended prematurely, then the current token can be a field.\n\nIf the preamble fails to compile for another reason, or if the preamble\ndoes compile, then the current token cannot be a field. (In the grammar,\na nonempty valid filter has to be followed by some kind of operator, not\nanother field.)\n\nImprove 967a3c3df94d09a09306a23ae248ef611f57087b / #12811",
  "state": "merged",
